---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="StockSummarizer is a research-clarity brand: plain-English stock, sector, and market briefs for DIY investors."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold">About StockSummarizer</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-muted">
      We turn noisy market data into plain-English summaries so everyday DIY investors can decide faster, with less overwhelm.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-[1.05rem] leading-7">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Who it’s for</h2>
      <p>
        Retail and DIY investors who research their own picks — comfortable buying individual stocks or ETFs, but short on time.
        You want understanding more than hot tips.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">What we do</h2>
      <p>
        We analyze and summarize individual stocks, sectors, and the broader market in clear, structured briefs.
        Unlike tipsters, meme-stock hype, or dense institutional research, we explain <em>what happened</em>,
        <em>why it matters</em>, and <em>what to watch next</em> — without pretending to pick winners for you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Brand promise</h2>
      <p>Every brief leaves you clearer than you started — in minutes, not hours.</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Consistent structure so you know what you’ll get</li>
        <li>Plain language; jargon explained carefully</li>
        <li>Sourced claims — no mystery “sources say”</li>
        <li>Explicit “not financial advice” framing</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Voice</h2>
      <p><strong>Clear. Grounded. Useful.</strong> Calm and direct — specific numbers and catalysts, honest about uncertainty.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">How we stay free</h2>
      <p>
        Briefs are free and not paywalled. We plan to support the site with tasteful ads, disclosed affiliate partnerships,
        and optional digital ebooks/guides. See <a href="/disclosures/">disclosures</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
